<title>ITALY: Italy banks to fall into line on rates - Bank Assoc..</title>
<headline>Italy banks to fall into line on rates - Bank Assoc..</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>All of Italy's banks will have adjusted their borrowing and lending rates by the end of the month following the Bank of Italy's 75 basis point cut in the discount rate in January, a top Italian banker said.</p>
<p>&quot;By the end of March the system will have reduced rates by 0.75 percent,&quot; said Tancredi Bianchi, President of the Italian banking association (ABI).</p>
<p>Bianchi said that lending rates had fallen 0.27 percent in January.</p>
<p>He said that market expectations of further interest rate cuts had been shaken &quot;by this contretemps on the monetary union front.&quot;</p>
<p>Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
</text>
